commentBody:
@Steve L
I’m forever bemused by the behemoth portions that seem to be the norm in the US. Yes, you can take uneaten food home (not so simple if you’re a tourist) but why doesn’t that beg the question ‘who needs portions that are too large for one meal?’  Would it not be better and cheaper to provide a reasonable portion that can be comfortably eaten at that meal? 
Yours, in confusion.

@Bill 

I'm not even close to being a fast solver...generally a Saturday puzzle takes me s little over an hour... but my record for a Saturday is around nineteen minutes, because I solved one ridiculously easy Saturday puzzle (or maybe just particularly in my wheelhouse) in the archives. Consistently matching difficulty to the appropriate day of the week must be difficult, especially since difficulty is partly determined by the solver's particular vocabulary and past experiences, so I cut them as much slack as they need.

I look at it kind of like lunch time in elementary school; you show up at the cafeteria and you take whaterver you're served that day.

@Helen Wright

A few years back I gave myself permission to look up a chart of the Greek alphabet when a crossword calls for that knowledge.

Maybe I'll go ahead and memorize it at some point, but since that information is available with a few taps on my phone it seems about as useful as memorizing the first hundred digits of pi...impressive in s way, but pointless.

@B
You’re right…I shouldn’t have said “I wonder” because I know plenty feel the same way.  I guess I was referring more to those who loathe them enough to want them gone, like “let’s sign a petition, let’s enact a law, let’s…”—level of loathing.

Ok, now I’ve solidified my reputation as one of the “those complainers”.🤦🏻‍♀️
